# Player and admin login.
::case login.player  A player connects and lands in their location
::login alice Alice alicepass
think [name(%#)]
think [loc(%#)]
look
::case login.admin  A wizard connects
::login wiz Wiz wizpass
think [name(%#)] [hasflag(%#,WIZARD)]
::case login.god  God connects
::login god One godpass
think [name(%#)] [hasflag(%#,WIZARD)] [hasflag(%#,ROYALTY)]
::case login.badpassword  A wrong password is refused
::login-fail bad Alice wrong
::case login.unknown  An unknown player is refused
::login-fail nobody Nobody whatever
::case login.warn-interval  no automatic building warnings arrive in the first minutes after startup
# PennMUSH's first automatic warning check comes warn_interval (1 hour by default) after startup
# (options.warn_counter, src/conf.c:1507; src/timer.c:186). This file runs first, while both servers are
# young, so God, who owns the fixture room, stays connected until each has been up 75 seconds.
::as god
::until WARNWAIT1
@wait [bound(sub(75,sub(secs(),convtime(starttime()))),0,15)]=think WARNWAIT1
::until WARNWAIT2
@wait [bound(sub(75,sub(secs(),convtime(starttime()))),0,15)]=think WARNWAIT2
::until WARNWAIT3
@wait [bound(sub(75,sub(secs(),convtime(starttime()))),0,15)]=think WARNWAIT3
::until WARNWAIT4
@wait [bound(sub(75,sub(secs(),convtime(starttime()))),0,15)]=think WARNWAIT4
::until WARNWAIT5
@wait [bound(sub(75,sub(secs(),convtime(starttime()))),0,15)]=think WARNWAIT5
